# Team Command Router

Use explicit team commands from the user to select the review workflow.

## Command Identification

Treat any of the following as an explicit team selection:
- `/custom-rule: team sql`
- `/custom-rule: team b2c`
- `/custom-rule: team de-matrix`
- `/custom-rule: team web-app`
- `/custom-rule: team presentation`
- `/custom-rule: team auto`

Treat any of the following as an explicit reset:
- `/custom-rule: team reset`

If the user gives multiple teams in one request, ask which one to run first.

## Session Team Lock (Sticky Mode)

Maintain `Active Team` for the whole current chat session.

- On explicit team selection, set `Active Team` to that team.
- On messages without team selection, reuse `Active Team`.
- Keep using `Active Team` until the user explicitly switches or resets it.
- On reset, clear `Active Team` and return to normal selection flow.

When `Active Team` is set, do not auto-switch by intent inference.
If `Active Team` is not set:
- if the request clearly matches one team, select it and state the inferred choice
- if intent is ambiguous, ask a short clarification question

## Dialog Window Binding

Treat ledgers as bound to **`DW-*` dialog window** and **`project_id`**.

- Resolve `project_id` from repo; resolve `dialog_window_id` (`DW-NNN`) from `.dialog_window_lock` (see DCI skill).
- Before load: verify `.project_lock` + `.dialog_window_lock` + `dialogs/DW-NNN/dialog_index.md` headers.
- On project mismatch: refuse load (exit 2). On window mismatch: refuse load (exit 2).
- **Window-scoped:** `Q-*`, `CL-*`, `TH-*`, window `CP-*` — reuse IDs only within same `DW-*`.
- **Project-scoped:** `EV-PROJECT`, `EV-*`, project `CP-*` in `project_catalog.md` — shared across windows; expand explicitly.
- New Cursor chat → `/custom-rule: dci restore-new "<summary>"`.
- Project/window tree in current repo → `/custom-rule: dci windows` (EV branches + DW summaries).
- Multi-project overview → `/custom-rule: dci projects`.
- Save/compress context → `/custom-rule: dci compress`; run `bash .cursor/tools/dci/bin/dci-vector.sh compress` only (pipeline: materialize + doctor + validate + sync); output = script stdout (`---` + `restore:`), **never** manual `Conclusion/Project Evolution Ledger` tables as compress result; **never** auto `--force` without user consent on hash_embed blocker.
- Switch window → `/custom-rule: dci restore DW-NNN` (slim: delta + hot_open, not full bundle).
- Heal ledger происходит автоматически внутри `/custom-rule: dci compress` (materialize + doctor + validate + sync). Отдельный `doctor` — debug-only fallback для инженерной диагностики.
- After compress in chat → load **delta only** (`dialogs/DW-NNN/dialog_delta.md`); do not read archive bundle.
- `/custom-rule: team reset` resets team lock only; does not clear ledgers.
- Explicit ledger reset: `/custom-rule: dci reset-ledger`.

## Skill Routing

When `/custom-rule: team sql` is selected, follow `.cursor/skills/sql-team/SKILL.md`.
When `/custom-rule: team b2c` is selected, follow `.cursor/skills/b2c-team/SKILL.md`.
When `/custom-rule: team de-matrix` is selected, follow `.cursor/skills/de-matrix-team/SKILL.md`.
When `/custom-rule: team web-app` is selected, follow `.cursor/skills/web-app-team/SKILL.md`.
When `/custom-rule: team presentation` is selected, follow `.cursor/skills/presentation-team/SKILL.md`.
When `/custom-rule: team auto` is selected, perform auto-selection:
- choose `presentation` if the request is about presentation, slides, storytelling, diagrams, infographics, visual narrative, business value communication, or technical architecture communication for stakeholders
- choose `web-app` if the request is about web ui, frontend plus backend app development, docker or kubernetes runtime, cicd gates, deployment, security hardening, monitoring, scaling, and full sdlc delivery
- choose `de-matrix` if the request is about competency matrix, assessment criteria, certification/attestation tracks, skills framework, grading rubric, or role-level requirements
- choose `b2c` if the task includes Java/Scala/Spark/Hive/HDFS, YAML pipeline config (`ctl.yaml`, `mart.yaml`), or mixed SQL plus JVM stack
- choose `sql` if the task is SQL-only (Greenplum/PostgreSQL 9.4), SQL objects, SQL performance, SQL documentation, or SQL business logic validation
- if evidence is still ambiguous, ask one short clarification question before selecting
- always state the selection as `Selected Team (auto): <team>` with one-line rationale, then execute that team's skill

When `Active Team` is reused (no new explicit command), start with:
`Selected Team (locked): <team>`.

## Token-Efficient Context Reuse

Maintain a lightweight `Conclusion Ledger` for the current chat.

- Assign stable IDs to finalized conclusions: `CL-001`, `CL-002`, ...
- Reuse existing conclusions by ID instead of repeating full rationale.
- For repeated topics, return delta-only updates (what changed and why).

Support these explicit user intents:
- `/custom-rule: dci reuse` -> reuse prior conclusions by default
- `/custom-rule: dci challenge <CL-id or topic>` -> criticize or dispute selected conclusions
- `/custom-rule: dci confirm <CL-id or topic>` -> verify and confirm selected conclusions
- `/custom-rule: dci refresh <CL-id or topic>` -> re-evaluate selected conclusions from scratch

Decision policy:
- Full overlap and no new evidence -> reuse existing conclusion IDs, no full rewrite
- Partial overlap -> keep unchanged IDs, update only impacted IDs
- Contradiction with new evidence -> mark old ID as superseded and create new ID

## Project Evolution Ledger

Maintain a compact `Project Evolution Ledger` linked to `Conclusion Ledger`.

- Assign stable evolution IDs: `EV-001`, `EV-002`, ...
- For each evolution item, store: scope, delta summary, key points, and linked conclusion IDs (`CL-*`).
- Mark evolution domain explicitly: `sql`, `b2c`, `web-app`, `presentation`, or `cross-domain`.
- Track branch status for impacted workstreams: `active`, `in_progress`, `merged`, `dead`.
- Keep dead branches in history with closure reason and replacement reference if any.
- Keep in-progress branches with open risks and next checkpoint (`CP-*` in DCI).

Support these explicit user intents:
- `/custom-rule: evo report` -> short timeline of relevant `EV-*` with linked `CL-*`
- `/custom-rule: evo diff <EV-id|CL-id|topic>` -> focused diff/delta for selected scope
- `/custom-rule: evo branch-status` -> same data as `/custom-rule: dci windows` (DCI branch tree); no duplicate branch rows
- `/custom-rule: evo regress <EV-id|range|topic>` -> regression-oriented impact review over selected changes

Output policy:
- Prefer delta over full retelling.
- Reuse `EV-*` and `CL-*` IDs whenever possible.
- If evidence is missing, report uncertainty explicitly instead of inventing change history.

## Question Traceability

Maintain processed question IDs and links:

- Assign question IDs: `Q-001`, `Q-002`, ...
- Link every `Q-*` to related `CL-*` and `EV-*`.
- Keep this map compact to avoid repeating the same reasoning.
- On follow-up questions, reference `Q-*` first, then only delta updates.

## Memory Backend Strategy (chosen)

Use a hybrid memory strategy optimized for this project.

**DCI extension:** follow `.cursor/rules/dialog-context-index.mdc` (trigger) and `.cursor/skills/dialog-context-index/SKILL.md` (full protocol) for indexing, handoff, delta load modes, `CP-*`, `TH-*`, accompaniment v2, and `bash .cursor/tools/dci/bin/dci-vector.sh` (compress/windows/restore/projects/validate).

**TIG extension (code/repo context):** follow `.cursor/rules/tig-preflight-enforced.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/tig-snapshot.mdc` (both `alwaysApply`). Artifacts: `.cursor/context/tig/tig_snapshot.md` (structure map, reuse via fingerprint) + `.cursor/context/tig/tig_delta.md` (git diffs, always refresh). Commands: `bash .cursor/tools/tig/bin/tig-context.sh` preflight / `--delta-only` postflight. **Not** the same as DCI `dialog_delta.md` or compress snapshot.

| Layer | Artifact | Scope | Reuse |
|-------|----------|-------|-------|
| TIG | `.cursor/context/tig/tig_delta.md` → `.cursor/context/tig/tig_snapshot.md` | repo code structure + git evolution | snapshot reuse; delta refresh |
| DCI | `dialog_delta.md` → `dialog_index.md` | dialog ledgers Q/CL/EV | compress handoff |

Read order for implementation: **TIG delta first**, then TIG snapshot sections (Module map, Directory tree, File index), then DCI ledgers if team workflow active.

- Primary layer (always): structured in-dialog ledgers (`Q-*`, `CL-*`, `EV-*`, plus DCI `CP-*`, `TH-*`) scoped by **project_id** (repo-local `.cursor/context/`).
- Semantic layer (optional): embeddings index for long dialogs or cross-dialog import.
- Preferred backend: `pgvector` (best operational fit for SQL-first stack and simple deployment).
- Embeddings baseline: `text-embedding-3-small`; use lower dimensions for cost control when recall remains acceptable.
- Vector metadata filters must include: `project_id`, `dialog_id`, `team`, `ledger_type`, `branch_state`.
- If semantic layer is disabled or unavailable, continue with structured ledgers only.

Supported intents:
- `/custom-rule: dci semantic on` -> enable semantic retrieval mode
- `/custom-rule: dci semantic off` -> force structured-only mode
- `/custom-rule: dci semantic lookup <query>` -> retrieve related ledger records
- `/custom-rule: dci import-ledger <source>` -> import prior dialog summary with ID remapping

## Execution Contract

For all teams:
- **Implementation tasks:** TIG preflight/postflight per `tig-preflight-enforced.mdc` (unless user skips TIG).
- Keep role outputs separated by responsibility.
- Let roles discuss disagreements explicitly.
- On team activation, Registry Steward starts ledgers immediately (`Q-*`, `CL-*`, `EV-*`).
- Update `Conclusion Ledger` and `Project Evolution Ledger` for each meaningful delta.
- Ensure question traceability updates (`Q-*` -> `CL-*` -> `EV-*` -> `CP-*` -> `TH-*`) for each meaningful update.
- Require arbiter resolution for every unresolved dispute.
- Do not finalize until all blocking disputes are resolved.
- Keep context recap short: cite conclusion IDs and only include changed details.
- Keep evolution recap short: cite `EV-*` and `CL-*`, include only key deltas and branch state changes.
- End with a concise consensus summary and concrete next actions.

For `/custom-rule: team sql` and `/custom-rule: team b2c`:
- Require tester to select stand(s) from project context and report stand run results.
- Require tester to report functional test coverage and outcomes for critical scenarios.
- Require tester to use the mandatory mini-template defined in the selected team skill.
- Require tester QA gate (`pass`, `pass_with_risk`, `fail`) before finalization.
- Treat tester blocking defects as blockers until resolved or explicitly accepted by arbiter.

For `/custom-rule: team de-matrix`:
- Require technical writer to convert engineering discussion into clear human-readable technical language.
- Require reviewer to verify result alignment with competency-matrix scope and attestation context.
- Before matrix design/review, require using both guidance documents:
  - `exls_matrix/matrix_methodology.md`
  - `exls_matrix/middle_de_research_notes.md`

For `/custom-rule: team web-app`:
- Require reviewer to validate result alignment with full-cycle web app delivery scope.
- Require critic to challenge assumptions, architecture trade-offs, and hidden risks.
- Require technical writer to produce implementation-facing documentation and runbooks.

For `/custom-rule: team presentation`:
- **Mandatory full roster from session start (18 roles):** Business Owner, Technical User, Copywriter, **Designer (дизайнер)**, Layout Designer (верстальщик), SQL Engineer, Data Engineer, DevOps Engineer, UI/UX Designer, Architect, Technical Writer, Presentation Developer, Diagram and Infographic Specialist, Reviewer, Censor, Language and Context Checker, Arbiter, Registry Steward. All roles must contribute before delivery; no reduced team unless user explicitly requests.
- Follow `.cursor/skills/presentation-team/SKILL.md` section **Presentation Composition Methodology (Mandatory)**.
- Follow project rule `.cursor/rules/presentation-team-methodology.mdc` when present.
- Require business owner to validate ROI framing, pilot gates, and buyer decision criteria.
- Require technical user to validate end-user workflows, prerequisites, and realistic scenarios.
- Require copywriter to remove filler and duplication; sharpen headlines and CTA; no meta phrases in titles.
- Require **designer (дизайнер)** to define palette, cover art direction, and bigtech visual tone before layout implementation.
- Require layout designer (верстальщик) to validate slide density (75–90% fill), typography scale (body ≥10pt), and composition for projection/PDF.
- Require presentation developer to implement visual system: stroke SVG icons (no emoji), reusable layout components (`scenario-bar`, `roles-grid`, etc.).
- Require diagram and infographic specialist to ensure accurate and readable visual models.
- Require reviewer to run mandatory QA checklist (fill, font, layout, infographics, duplication, audience coverage, pilot criteria) before `pass`.
- Require censor and language-context checker to validate orthography, `е`/`ё` policy when specified, and semantic consistency.
